cite1†Skip to main content L1: \nL2: Menu\nL3: \nL4: # Exploding Lakes in Cameroon\nL5: \nL6: By cite2†Volcano Hazards Program March 14, 2016\nL7: \nL8: cite3†Image: Image: Exploding Lakes in Cameroon†d9-wret.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com L9: \nL10: cite4†Original†d9-wret.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com L11: ### Detailed Description\nL12: \nL13: In 1986, Lake Nyos, in the volcanic region of Cameroon, released a cloud of CO_{2} into the atmosphere, killing 1,700 people and 3,500 livestock in nearby towns and villages. Since then, engineers have been artificially removing the gas from the lake through piping. This photo shows a pipe top and raft at Lake Nyos. The self-driven fountain (inset) can reach a height of 150 feet above the lake surface while dissipating carbon dioxide.\nL14: \nL15: ### Sources/Usage\nL16: \nL17: Public Domain.\nL18: ###\nL19: \nL20: Photographer\nL21: \nL22: ### Explore Search\nL23: \nL24:   * cite5†Natural Hazards L25:   * cite6†volcanoes L26:   * cite7†Lake Nyos L27:   * cite8†Cameroon L28:   * cite9†Africa L29:   * cite10†monitoring L30:   * cite11†carbonDioxide L31:   * cite12†volcano L32:   * cite13†LakeNyos L33:   * cite14†Volcano Hazards Program L34:   * cite15†Office of Communications L35: \nL36: cite16†View All L37: \nL38: Was this page helpful?\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHedonism (Stanford Encyclopedia of Philosophy/Summer 2012 Edition) (https://plato.stanford.edu/archives/sum2012/entries/hedonism/)\nciteturn11view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn3search0\",\"pattern\":\"\"}); Total lines: 171\nNo matching text found for \"\""
